From b366bd19bffcd97d2e991bf22280fb070bbe41e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:47:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(update-pause): a paused turn whose record its
 live writer closed still continues in place

hermes-hub 2026-11-12: two headless kanban-notice turns in the gateway paused for a
core update; the detached-turn reaper closed their records 60 s later, the in-place
watcher read the closed record as 'the user moved on' and quit, and every reader
skipped the marker because its writer (the gateway) was alive. Both turns waited
60-70 min, with no 'window ended' line and no stuck WARNING, until the next gateway
restart.

A closed record is no longer 'busy' while the marker is still this process's own
pause: the watcher keeps watching (STUCK_WARN fires) and, when the window ends,
re-opens the chat here via session.resume from the stored source, which schedules
the continuation. A pause another process rewrote, or a chat in no store, ends the
watch; a refused re-open is retried each poll.
